{
  "_comment": [
    "THE MAP (ADR 0096). Coordinates are metres in the map's frame, Y up; the combat plane is y = 0.",
    "systems: where each system disc sits on the plane. highways: a centre-line as waypoints",
    "with a corner radius per waypoint (0 at an open end), two carriageways side by side,",
    "traffic on the right. planet_ramps: an exit and an entry on each carriageway at that",
    "system, shaped by the ramp rule in RoadNetwork from the exploration/ramp_* tuning keys.",
    "ramps: interchanges, authored as the waypoints BETWEEN the standard exit head and the",
    "standard merge tail; 'near' or 'at'+'offset' says where on the carriageway each end is,",
    "and 'mirror_of'+'about' turns a ramp half a turn about a system to serve the reverse",
    "carriageways. Saving this file relays the map out under the ship. The gate (and the",
    "console on load) names any bend that is too tight, any ramp that touches a road it does",
    "not join, and any highway that pitches too steeply.",
    "A highway may carry mouth_height (m above the plane) and mouth_along (m from the system centre) to move its planet mouths; K-112 rides 240 m above A-377B and its mouths at B sit higher and further out so its ramps pass over A-377B's.",
    "Scaled x2 on 2026-09-07: every distance doubled and cruise speed with it, so pacing is unchanged and everything far away is half the size against the ships and the tube, which did not scale."
